// Package v1alpha1 contains the Go API types for Grid CRDs at grid.praxis.fast/v1alpha1.
//
// These types are generated from the deployed CRD schemas in deploy/crds/*.yaml
// (themselves produced from the canonical Rust definitions in crates/operator/src/crd).
// The generator is cmd/gen-types. After make generate-crds, run make generate-go-types
// and make go-types-check to keep the generated files in sync.
//
// # Usage with controller-runtime
//
//	import v1alpha1 "github.com/praxis-proxy/grid/go/api/v1alpha1"
//
//	func init() {
//	    utilruntime.Must(v1alpha1.AddToScheme(scheme))
//	}
//
// # Compatibility and version skew
//
// Typed clients must still use narrow patch operations when modifying resources
// in a cluster that may have a newer version of the Grid CRD schema installed.
//
// A full-object update (client.Update, a PUT-equivalent) serialises only the
// fields declared in this module. Any field introduced by a newer installed
// schema  -  but absent from these types  -  will be silently dropped from the live
// object. These generated types provide compile-time checking; they do not
// prevent field loss from version skew.
//
// To avoid unintended field loss:
//
//   - Prefer server-side apply ([types.ApplyPatchType]) and declare only the
//     fields your controller owns. SSA merges your intent with fields set by
//     other managers rather than replacing the full object.
//   - Avoid Replace (client.Update) on resources that other controllers or
//     users may have extended with fields not present in this module version.
//   - After upgrading the Grid operator, update this module to a release that
//     includes the new schema fields before performing any full-object updates.
//
// # Generation and drift detection
//
// The types in this package are generated by cmd/gen-types from the deployed
// CRD schemas in deploy/crds/*.yaml. After every "make generate-crds" run:
//
//  1. make generate-go-types   -  regenerates zz_generated_*.go
//  2. make go-types-check      -  runs serialization and structural-drift tests
//
// A test failure indicates a field was added, renamed, or structurally changed
// in the Rust CRD types and the Go types need to be regenerated to match.
//
package v1alpha1
